	<key>readme</key>
	<string>ec2 [words]   List EC2 instances for every profile and region, filter by name, instance id, IP or type (all words must match).
  Running instances first, then by name.
  ↩ open an SSM session in iTerm (running instances only)
  ⌘↩ copy private IP · ⌥↩ open the instance in the AWS console · ⌘C copy instance id · ⌘L details
  Error items: on an SSO profile with expired or invalid credentials, ↩ runs aws sso login --profile &lt;p&gt; in iTerm.

Configuration (Configure Workflow):
  AWS_PROFILES   comma-separated profiles (empty = aws configure list-profiles)
  AWS_REGIONS    comma-separated regions for every profile (empty = each profile's configured region)
  EC2_CACHE_SECONDS   how long instance lists and profile/region lookups are cached (default 300)

Needs /usr/local/bin/aws and /usr/local/bin/session-manager-plugin. Only read-only calls: ec2 describe-instances, aws configure get/list-profiles, and one sts get-caller-identity per profile when a region answers AuthFailure (to tell a region that is not enabled from bad credentials).
Cache: $alfred_workflow_cache (delete the files to force a refresh).
Tests: /usr/bin/python3 -B -m unittest test_ec2</string>
